<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · city</p><h1 class="enc-title">Riobamba</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Riobamba is a city in the central highlands of Ecuador, capital of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/chimborazo">Chimborazo</a> Province. Founded by the Spanish in 1534 in the land of the Puruhá, it was the first Spanish city in what is now Ecuador. After an earthquake destroyed it in 1797 it was rebuilt on a new site, and in 1830 it hosted the constituent assembly that drew up the first constitution of independent Ecuador.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/riobamba.jpg" alt="Riobamba" width="320" height="436" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: David C. S. · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Collage_Riobamba.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
